<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico sees export growth through 2000.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico sees export growth through 2000.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's exports will continue to grow consistently until the year 2000, the government said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Outlining economic projections in its National Program for Financing Development 1997-2000, the government also said that private consumption and total investment would continue to grow as well.</p>
<p>It forecast the following total exports from a base year of 1996 = 100.  </p>
<p>    YEAR		    AMOUNT</p>
<p>    1996		100.0</p>
<p>    1997		112.6</p>
<p>    1998		124.5</p>
<p>    1999		136.9</p>
<p>    2000		150.7</p>
<p>It forecast total investments, also from a base year of 1996 =100:</p>
<p>    YEAR		    AMOUNT</p>
<p>    1996		100.0 (actual)</p>
<p>    1997		114.5</p>
<p>    1998		126.7</p>
<p>    1999		139.9</p>
<p>    2000		154.8</p>
<p>It forecast private consumption as follows, as real annual growth:</p>
<p>    YEAR		    AMOUNT</p>
<p>    1996		    2.3 percent (actual)</p>
<p>    1997		    3.2 percent</p>
<p>    1998		    4.0 percent</p>
<p>    1999		    4.2 percent</p>
<p>    2000		    5.0 percent</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
